  "assessments": [
    {
      "topic": "zero reads and model notifications",
      "status": "PASS",
      "detail": "Each traffic combo changes only advance() revision/dirty and posts QObject-bound refresh. No date/request/session/frame/readRequested mutation or new IO is introduced. Existing snapshots remain bound; both exact model no-op paths suppress notifications for an unchanged binding. Explicit daily Payload summary/table values and seven-day table remain separate from selected chart family."
    },
    {
      "topic": "visibility and reentry",
      "status": "PASS",
      "detail": "Both refresh methods retain all current revision/QPointer/visible/minimized checks and only append traffic() to existing plot setter calls. Immediate revision invalidation prevents an older tooltip/accessibility refresh from later writing a stale model; queued refresh lets Qt combo setters finish and is canceled on deletion. Hidden/minimized changes defer chart/tooltip/model changes until activation."
    },
    {
      "topic": "constructor/default compatibility",
      "status": "PASS",
      "detail": "Daily adds third enum argument, Week fourth after the preserved bool. Both defaultPayload and validate initial enum before choosing combo index, before handlers are connected. Old callers therefore preserve date/resolution behavior and Payload. Labels/buddies and Chart traffic accessible names are present in enum order."
    },
    {
      "topic": "navigation capture/restore",
      "status": "PASS",
      "detail": "Two defaultPayload enum fields append after previous scalar fields; trivial copying remains enforced. Validator requires both enums; Page keeps complete all-or-default admission. Constructor forwards each independent saved choice and getter captures both hidden controls. Existing Window scalar record automatically carries these fields without retaining packets/widgets; closed-session policy remains unchanged."
    },
    {
      "topic": "old lifecycle/accounting scope",
      "status": "PASS",
      "detail": "55 pre-existing member definitions plus both full table models and all read/session/stale admission callbacks are exact. No worker/adapter/core/parser/accounting, new read, timer, configuration persistence, combined sum or Java equality scope is added."
    }
